PART 5 -- absolute levels, both footings, and the Upsilon lever measured
==========================================================================================================================
   routeA   a0(lo) = 2.300e-10 = canon +0.390 dex / alt +0.309 dex   |   a0(hi) = 2.505e-10 = canon +0.428 / alt +0.346
   fw       a0(lo) = 2.433e-10 = canon +0.415 dex / alt +0.333 dex   |   a0(hi) = 2.594e-10 = canon +0.443 / alt +0.361
  the KiDS points used sit at y = g_bar/a0 = 0.0013 - 0.0402: deep MOND throughout
  d log a0 / d log Upsilon, MEASURED by refitting with g_bar shifted +-0.1 dex: -1.062
  On the RATIO only the DIFFERENTIAL survives: d ln(ratio)/dz = -ln10 * d log Upsilon/dz, which at matched
  stellar mass is the residual z-evolution of the SED pipeline's own M/L, not the full M/L budget.
  [PASS] k01-6 the Upsilon lever is measured, not asserted, and it is the deep-MOND -1 (matching the -1.046 the veins sweep measured for the KiDS dwarf stack) -- so every ABSOLUTE a0 here is a stellar-mass measurement in a0's clothing and must not be quoted as a footing test   (measured -1.062 against the deep-MOND -1.000)

==========================================================================================================================
PART 6 -- mutation controls
==========================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M1 closure: replacing the high-z stack by the low-z one must give ln ratio exactly 0 with zero jackknife error   (ln ratio 0.000e+00 +- 0.000e+00)
  [PASS] M2 the mechanism control, demonstrated rather than argued: pairing a LOW stellar-mass bin at low z against a HIGH one at high z produces a large spurious a0 ratio in the direction the deep-MOND -1 lever predicts   (deliberate mismatch d logM = +0.593 dex gives ln ratio +0.5541 +- 0.2799, predicted by the lever alone -0.3171 to -1.3653; matched +0.0855)
  [PASS] M3 mutation: nu = 1 (baryons only, no boost) must be destroyed by these data   (chi2(nu=1) = 3.2e+03 / 2.63e+03 on 6 dof, against chi2(Route A) = 6.59 / 14.41)
  [PASS] M4 injection closure at an injected a0 ratio of 1.00: the pipeline recovers it without bias   (injected ln +0.0000, recovered -0.0072 +- 0.0101 (per-realisation sd 0.1755))
  [PASS] M4 injection closure at an injected a0 ratio of 1.30: the pipeline recovers it without bias   (injected ln +0.2624, recovered +0.2636 +- 0.0091 (per-realisation sd 0.1579))
  [PASS] M5 robustness AGAINST INTEREST: the extended cut must be reported beside the primary and the two must agree   (EXT +0.3246 +- 0.1786 (+2.845/z) vs REL +0.0855 +- 0.2367 (+0.750/z))
  [PASS] M6 kernel swap: at these accelerations (y < 0.05) Route A and nu = sqrt(1+1/y) are both in their deep-MOND limit, so the RATIO must be kernel-independent -- if it were not, the result would be a kernel artefact   (Route A +0.0855 vs fw +0.0641 (difference 0.0215); the ABSOLUTE levels differ by -0.024 dex, which is the kernel's normalisation)

