VERDICT (k01)
==========================================================================================================================
  The first MASS-MATCHED lensing a0(z).  Route A, REL cut, four absolute stellar-mass bins matched bin by bin
  in every g_bar bin by frozen harmonic weights; 50-patch patch-consistent jackknife.
     ln[a0(z=0.372)/a0(z=0.258)] = +0.0855 +- 0.2367  ->  ratio 1.089 +- 0.258
     d ln a0/dz = +0.750 +- 2.076 /z   [= +0.326 +- 0.902 dex/z]
  Unmatched, same data, same jackknife: ratio 1.333 +- 0.218, d ln a0/dz = +2.106 +- 1.503/z.
  The mass matching removes the systematic the banked note called decisive, and the answer does not become
  decisive: the statistics lost to matching cancel the systematics gained.  NOT Kepler-grade.
